  "explanation": "The proposal presents a well-scoped, highly practical empirical study investigating the faithfulness of language model explanations under minimal counterfactual rule changes. The experimental setup clearly specifies using Llama-3-8B-Instruct with 4-bit quantization on a single 12 GB GPU, and provides concrete pilot checks, data splitting, and evaluation methodologies.",
  "problems": [
    "KV cache and activation memory overhead during generation could push peak VRAM usage above the 11 GB threshold when processing longer reasoning traces under concurrent structured decoding constraints.",
    "Relying on auxiliary NLI models or regular expressions for semantic entailment checks may introduce parsing noise or false positives when detecting subtle logical rule adjustments."
  ],
  "improvements": [
    "Run a preliminary VRAM profiling test measuring peak memory consumption with KV caching enabled before executing the full 700-instance test split.",
    "Incorporate the deterministic symbolic verification oracle as the primary adjudication mechanism to bypass vulnerable auxiliary NLI entailment checks."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "passage_id": "s_804283a9e96852bfbc63",
      "claim": "LLMs can generate plausible explanations that are unfaithful to their underlying reasoning.",
      "relation": "supports"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "s_82484666fca05d79f910",
      "claim": "Correlational counterfactual tests assess explanation faithfulness by evaluating output shifts under input edits.",
      "relation": "supports"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "s_cf572350c76ccfdcb56b",
      "claim": "Prompting methods for logical reasoning suffer from unfaithfulness where conclusions do not align with reasoning chains.",
      "relation": "supports"
    }
  ],
  "uncertainty": "It remains unknown whether 4-bit quantized Llama-3-8B-Instruct with structured decoding will consistently avoid out-of-memory errors during long-form text generation within a 12 GB VRAM limit.",
  "tradeoffs": [
    "Using a smaller 8B model via 4-bit quantization fits comfortably within consumer hardware constraints but might limit complex multi-clause logical reasoning performance compared to larger unquantized models."
  ],
  "falsification_test": "If pilot VRAM profiling shows that activation memory and KV cache exceed 12 GB during generation, or if structured decoding parsing success drops below 95%, the experimental setup must reduce generation context length or switch to a smaller 3B instruction-tuned model."
}
